  "notes": "The research calls this \"jazz-loop rap with an actual low-end doctrine\", and the doctrine is a set of tradeoffs the model has to make in both directions at once. The bass is the featured instrument, so it gets the widest register in this batch — [28,52], a full two octaves — the lowest `followRootsProb` here at 0.35, and six passing tones, because \"walking or riffing with real melodic content\" is a melodic part with a bass clef. Everything else gets out of its way: `velocityTiers.main` drops to 70–84 because the drums are thin *on purpose*, `percs` runs two lanes at [0,1], `melody.densityPerBar` is [2,5] for the deliberately sparse mid-range, and `hihat.fillDensity` is 0.38. The kick is the one grammar change from the archetype — the research says \"kick 1 and the 4th 8th\", so `secondaryAnchor` is `2&`, not the boom-bap `3&`. Harmony is 7th/9th/11th colour on ii–V–i, i–iv and genuine one-chord modal vamps (the bare-`i` family is researched here, not inferred), with `ninth` at 0.34. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it high-medium: the album-level making-of and the live-bass session are documented, but the tempo band and the drum velocities are read off the catalogue. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 52 to 47 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 48 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 5.",
